Spec: Scheduler

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the collection and delivery processes, and provide an IPC credential broker.

Platform: Go/Linux

References:
  ../../mitm-2.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Must:
  The IPC Server listens on a Unix Domain Socket for events and credential requests.
  Respond to `{"type": "get_credentials"}` requests by returning the in-memory KEK and Database JSON configuration.
  Not pass the DB credentials or KEK via environment variables to spawned child processes.
  Handle and persist `status` and `audit` events received via IPC from child processes.
  All HTTP endpoints must strictly enforce authentication, and all RBAC management endpoints must enforce administrative authorization.

Exposes:
  /admin/dashboard/stats

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Enforce authentication and administrative authorization on all RBAC management endpoints, including /admin/rbac/os_user_roles.
  [x] #2 Feature: Issue #4 - Expose /admin/dashboard/stats returning DB info and DLQ count
  [x] #3 Bug: Issue #2 - Fix missing version info in /info API by correcting build script and adding a fallback
